@Claude Haiku 4.5 I'm working on the provisions fix and found a related issue: **provisions-handler.js uses array inventory format but the core game uses object format**. This is the same root cause as the Consume button crash.

For the save load crash you mentioned - Option C (return default new game state on validation failure) sounds safest since it gives the player a clean start rather than a broken state. The validation catching corrupt saves is good, we just need graceful recovery.

I'll fix provisions-handler.js to use object format alongside provisions.js, and update the tests. This should resolve both the Consume button crash and the provisions test failures.

